            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Alexandria to Philadelphia? </h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 2 hours 48 minutes to 2 hours 55 minutes, depending on the service (Northeast Regional, Carolinian, or Palmetto) and the number of stops. </p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Alexandria to Philadelphia? </h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Northeast Regional, which can complete the journey in approximately 2 hours 41 minutes to 2 hours 44 minutes with direct service. </p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Alexandria to Philadelphia cost? </h3>
            <p>
                Ticket prices generally fall between:
                $23-$40 for Northeast Regional Coach (early booking)
                $40-$80 for Northeast Regional Coach (standard)
                $60-$120 for Northeast Regional Business
                $30-$90 for Carolinian/Palmetto Coach
                $90-$200+ for last-minute or flexible fares
            </p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Alexandria to Philadelphia? </h3>
            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Northeast Regional, Carolinian, and Palmetto trains on this segment are direct, so there's no need for transfers. </p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard? </h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, free Wi-Fi, power outlets, a café car, and luggage space. Business Class includes complimentary non-alcoholic beverages and priority boarding. </p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving? </h3>
            <p>While driving on I-95 may take 2.5-3.5 hours, depending on traffic, the train is generally reliable and stress-free, especially during rush hour, when I-95 congestion is notorious. </p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Alexandria to Philadelphia in one day? </h3>
            <p>Yes, the route is well-suited for same-day trips, with 11-12 daily departures. Early morning trains get you to Philadelphia by mid-morning, and evening trains return you to Alexandria by late night. </p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Alexandria do trains depart from? </h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Alexandria Union Station, located in historic Old Town Alexandria. Airport connections exist via Metro from DCA and IAD. </p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Philadelphia? </h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Philadelphia William H. Gray III 30th Street Station, conveniently located in University City/Center City and easily accessible by SEPTA, trolley, and rideshare. </p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class worth it for this 2.5-3 hour trip? </h3>
            <p>For the 2.5-3 hour Alexandria-Philadelphia journey, Coach offers excellent value. Business Class is worthwhile for travelers who need a quiet, productive environment with complimentary beverages and extra legroom, but its moderate duration makes it optional rather than essential. </p>



